ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
\textbf{Solution:} Given an isosceles right triangle OAB with a hypotenuse of 1, constructing a square $A_{1}B_{1}C_{1}D_{1}$,

\(\therefore \angle A = \angle B = \angle AA_{1}D_{1} = \angle BB_{1}C_{1} = 45^\circ\), AO=BO, $A_{1}D_{1} = D_{1}C_{1} = B_{1}C_{1}$,

\(\therefore AD_{1} = A_{1}D_{1} = D_{1}C_{1} = A_{1}B_{1} = C_{1}B\),

\(\therefore\) The edge length of the square $A_{1}B_{1}C_{1}D_{1}$ is $A_{1}B_{1} = \frac{1}{3}AB = \frac{1}{3}\);

Similarly, the edge length of the square $A_{2}B_{2}C_{2}D_{2}$ is $A_{2}B_{2} = \left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{2}$;

The edge length of the square $A_{3}B_{3}C_{3}D_{3}$ is $A_{3}B_{3} = \left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{3}$;

\(\therefore\) The edge length of the 5th square $A_{5}B_{5}C_{5}D_{5}$ is \(\boxed{\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{5}}\).

